---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { events, formatLong, lastUpdated } from '../data/record';
---
<PageLayout
  title="About"
  heading="An open record of AI risk"
  description="How SafeAI.watch chooses and reads its sources, and what its record of AI safety and security covers."
  intro="SafeAI.watch collects public research, reported incidents, warnings, and policy on AI safety and security. Each entry links its source and states the limits of its evidence."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <section id="method" aria-labelledby="method-heading">
      <h2 id="method-heading">How entries are read</h2>
      <p>
        Each entry starts with what happened and who reported it. It then says what the evidence
        supports and what remains unresolved. The date on an entry is the date its linked source
        was published.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="sources" aria-labelledby="sources-heading">
      <h2 id="sources-heading">Evidence and attribution</h2>
      <p>
        Company reports give the company's own findings. Preprints may change before peer review.
        Court filings contain allegations a court has not yet tested. Essays and interviews present
        arguments and forecasts. News reports give an account readers can check against the original
        material.
      </p>
      <p>
        A capability shown in a controlled test, a warning about future harm, and an observed incident
        are different kinds of evidence. A serious warning can justify scrutiny while its likelihood
        remains uncertain.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="scope" aria-labelledby="scope-heading">
      <h2 id="scope-heading">Scope of the record</h2>
      <p>
        The record covers AI safety and security: research and evaluations, reported incidents,
        public warnings and statements, and policy. It began with AI and biological risk.
      </p>
      <p>
        It holds {events.length} entries, a selection of sources published through{' '}
        <time datetime={lastUpdated}>{formatLong(lastUpdated)}</time>. It does not cover every
        development or track events as they happen.
      </p>
      <p>
        The featured GZERO World interview is linked editorial coverage. It is not an endorsement of this
        project. Illustrations are conceptual artwork and contain no measured results.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="further" aria-labelledby="further-heading">
      <h2 id="further-heading">Reading further</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="/latest">Browse the source archive</a> or <a href="/timeline">follow the timeline</a>.
        Each source link leads to the original, where readers can check its context, revisions, and
        later developments.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="typefaces" aria-labelledby="typefaces-heading">
      <h2 id="typefaces-heading">Typefaces</h2>
      <p>
        The site is set in Geist and Geist Mono by Vercel and Newsreader by Production Type. All three
        are served from this site under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. Licence texts: <a href="/licenses/OFL-Geist.txt">Geist</a>,{' '}
        <a href="/licenses/OFL-Geist-Mono.txt">Geist Mono</a>, <a href="/licenses/OFL-Newsreader.txt">Newsreader</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
